<title>THAILAND: Thailand says to cooperate with Australia on sugar.</title>
<headline>Thailand says to cooperate with Australia on sugar.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand and Australia are set to cooperate in seeking reduced import tariffs on sugar exports to Japan and South Korea, Thai Cane and Sugar Board secretary general Pramote Vidtayasuk said on Monday.</p>
<p>Cooperation between the Thai Cane and Sugar Board and Australia's Queenland's Sugar Corp would also cover areas such as sales strategies, he told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to hold a meeting with them soon. As major sugar exporting countries, there are lots we can do together,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Pramote said Japan and South Korea had been big markets for Thailand and Australia. However, tariffs on sugar, especially whites, were very high.</p>
<p>Japan and South Korea normally imported only raw sugar and refine locally.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe we can boost trade to these two countries if the tariff were lower,&quot; Pramote said without elaborating further.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
